          "id": "kb-af831486a59b976ffa16a9ab483529de17c7d77f05c0f51c74e8dd9dfea6bac0",
          "url": "https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Reference/Status/404",
          "text": "# 404 Not Found\n\nThe HTTP **`404 Not Found`** [client error response](/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Reference/Status#client_error_responses) status code indicates that the server cannot find the requested resource. Links that lead to a 404 page are often called broken or dead links and can be subject to [link rot](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Link_rot \"External link (opens in new tab)\").\n\nA 404 status code only indicates that the resource is missing without indicating if this is temporary or permanent. If a resource is permanently removed, servers should send the [`410 Gone`](/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Reference/Status/410) status instead.",
          "title": "404 Not Found - HTTP | MDN",
